    fix(repo_loader): expand workspace member globs to concrete dirs

    workspace_members stored the raw `[workspace].members` patterns (e.g. ruff's
    `crates/*`), but both consumers prefix-match them against concrete root paths
    (lib_root_member_dir, crate_name_for_root). A glob never prefix-matches
    `crates/ruff_db/src/lib.rs`, so on ruff EVERY lib root returned None ->
    crate_deps_by_root was EMPTY -> the cross-crate fallback never fired (+0 recovery,
    byte-identical to main). Fix: record each parsed `[package]` manifest's concrete
    dir (prism already walks every member Cargo.toml into manifest_hashes) instead of
    the declared patterns. Verified on ruff: crate_deps_by_root populates;
    recovery_typepath.singleton 260 -> 298 (+38), multi_target_exact_sites unchanged
    (46, no new collision FPs). All 5 plan-review rounds + every test used CONCRETE
    synthetic workspace_members, so the glob case was unexercised until the real-corpus
    call-stats acceptance. New repo_loader test glob_workspace_members_expand_to_concrete_dirs
    pins it. --lib 360 (no crate_name_for_root/extern-crate regression).

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

